# Generation 3, round 1, H3 (generations/gen003/PLAN.md, version 1). Storm share of the week's residual move.
# e = the coin's hourly return net of its rolling hourly beta to the unit's equal-weighted mean return m (beta
# = corr x std ratio over the last n hourly rows). Weekly bins run Monday 00:00 to Sunday 23:00 UTC (bar opens);
# a bin is visible at the bar that opens Sunday 23:00 and is traded at the Monday 00:00 open, so the weights
# change once a week. vol = the bin's residual hourly volatility; x = the bin's mean of e over vol (the week's
# residual move); y = the bin's mean of the conditioned part over vol; z = y net of a cross-sectional fit on x,
# orthogonal to the week's residual move across coins on every bin. Short the largest z, long the smallest;
# dollar neutral, gross 1. No funding, mark or index input.
# The conditioned part: e times s, s = BTC's squared hourly return over its own trailing k-hour mean square (the
# hour's share of BTC's recent variance, the same for every coin in an hour): the residual move made in hours
# when BTC moved far more than usual weighs most, a calm hour little. e is net of each coin's own beta, so a
# high-beta coin's mechanical move in a storm is not the signal.
name = "gen003_storm_share"
family = "meanrev"
kind = "portfolio"
unit = "top30"
hypothesis = "Storm share: in hours of market stress, altcoin moves beyond beta come from forced deleveraging and thin liquidity, not coin news, so the part of a weekly residual move made in BTC storm hours partly reverses relative to the calm-hour part. Short coins with a large storm-hour part for their week, long a small one; weekly. Falsified if the DEV sign is wrong (never flipped), VAL PSR(0) < 0.90, 2x costs negative, no G6 timing, or next30 disagrees."

n = param(336, 268, 404)       # hours in the rolling hourly beta to the unit's mean return (14 days)
k = param(168, 134, 202)       # hours in the coin's own trailing norm (7 days)

r = ret(close, 1)
m = cs_mean(r)
e = r - corr(r, m, n) * std(r, n) / std(m, n) * m
vol = sqrt(tf_mean(e * e, weekly))
x = cs_demean(tf_mean(e, weekly) / vol)
rb = ret(btc(close), 1)
s = rb * rb / sma(rb * rb, k)
y = cs_demean(tf_mean(e * s, weekly) / vol)
b = cs_mean(x * y) / cs_mean(x * x)
z = y - b * x
signal = cs_scale(cs_demean(-cs_rank(z)))
